  "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\u222d}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V={\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{0}2y\\,dz]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{0}2y\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}[2yz]_{z=x}^{z=0}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2y(0-x)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}-2xy\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/10a5bb8e61589b71634a21dd17c342eb3f8212995aef52e28f8e8e8033fcdc7d.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}-2xy\\,dA & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2x}2xy\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{2+2x}2xy\\text{\u00a0}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2+2x}dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}x{(2+2x)}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4x+8{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & =-{[2{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =-0+(2-\\frac{8}{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
